        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Complex analysis is the study of functions of a complex variable. It is simultaneously one of the most elegant fields in pure mathematics and one of the most powerful tools in applied science. The surprise: imposing differentiability on complex functions is *far* more restrictive than on real functions. A once-differentiable complex function is automatically infinitely differentiable, equal to its own power series, and tightly constrained by its values on any curve."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#003",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:complex-analysis:00-overview, git-history:complex-analysis:00-overview]",
